 {}, "type": "CLIPTextEncode", "mode": 0, "bgcolor": "#63a3a3", "size": [360, 190], "pos": [7600, -490], "id": 4, "properties": {"cnr_id": "comfy-core", "hasSecondTab": false, "ver": "0.8.2", "ue_properties": {"widget_ue_connectable": {}, "input_ue_unconnectable": {}, "version": "7.8"}, "widget_ue_connectable": {"text": true}, "secondTabText": "Send Back", "enableTabs": false, "secondTabOffset": 80, "Node name for S&R": "CLIPTextEncode", "tabWidth": 65, "secondTabWidth": 65, "tabXOffset": 10}, "order": 6}, {"outputs": [{"name": "text", "links": [123], "label": "text", "type": "*", "localized_name": "text"}, {"name": "show_help", "label": "show_help", "type": "STRING", "localized_name": "show_help"}], "color": "#232", "widgets_values": ["An ancient teal-green Yinglong forms the larger geography of a vast mountain world. From an ordinary stone terrace within a secluded Chinese temple precinct, the viewer looks across a deep mist-filled ravine toward one immense, distant curve of the dragon’s body passing behind mountain cliffs. The body is so large that its dark green surface initially reads as another mountain wall; only a broad band of weathered scales, sparse dorsal ridges, and the far silhouette of its neck reveal that the landscape is alive.\n\nA cluster of traditional wooden halls, tiled roofs, narrow bridges, and ancient pines occupies one small ledge within the ravine, visibly connected to the terrain rather than arranged as foreground decoration. Far above the temple valley, the root of one enormous folded wing disappears into cloud layers, while the dragon’s head remains distant and partly obscured by the surrounding peaks. Soft daylight enters through broken clouds, creating pale jade light on wet stone, deep blue-green shadow in the ravine, and restrained aged-gold highlights on the temple roofs. Quiet sacred scale, ancient Chinese mythic landscape, cinematic painterly realism."], "inputs": [{"widget": {"name": "text"}, "name": "text", "label": "text", "ty